 "remarks": "NEW YORK CITY : Time to Move/Flee? Stamford has been named the safest city in Connecticut. The Quality of Life is far superior to Manhattan, and the average price of a home is about 1/5 the cost. A newer residence In Manhattan is about $2,000 per square foot. In Stamford, it's about $388 per square foot. Two Million Dollars will get you about 1,000 square ft 2 bedroom condo in Manhattan versus about 5,100 square feet in Stamford.It is the center of The Gold Coast and is surrounded by Three of the Richest Towns in AMERICA: Greenwich, Darien and New Canaan and only 35 miles away. Total Area:7,568 sq. ft.* Main Living Space: 5,285 sq. ft., Walk-Out Finished Basement: 2,283 sq. ft. with high ceilings, Bedrooms/Baths: 5+ spacious bedrooms, 5 marble-finished bathrooms, Oversized 3-car garage (30' x 15') with epoxy-coated floors, Corner of Woodbine Road & Reservoir Lane, steps from the scenic Laurel Reservoir, Grand two-story foyer with double curved staircases, Brick front with cedar siding and a new roof (5 years old) Dedicated in-law/nanny suite with private entrance on the main level, Expansive deck and huge storage shed, Three wood-burning fireplaces/stove, Hydro-Air Heating and A/C, Summer kitchen in the lower level - perfect for entertaining or large gatherings, Whole-house generator, Integrated security system (Oil Tank encapsulated in vault=leakproof), Lightning arrestor and whole-house water filtration system, LED lighting throughout . Agent Owned",
